        {
          "id": "55ed830d-595e-3f5f-a13a-d51cd5ac0f3e",
          "content": {
            "id": "55ed830d-595e-3f5f-a13a-d51cd5ac0f3e",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Volkswagen's third-quarter sales lifted by Europe and EVs",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Volkswagen Group's release of new models paid off in the third quarter.</p><p>The German auto giant reported a 1% rise in deliveries during the period on Friday.</p><p>It said a boost from Europe and South America pushed back on pressure from China and the U.S..</p><p>Group deliveries to China fell 7%.</p><p>VW isn't\u00a0the only German major to see a sales decline in the country recently.</p><p>Mercedes' was down by more than a quarter over the same period, while BMW also saw a slight drop.</p><p>Electric vehicles were a bright spot for VW in the third quarter.</p><p>Deliveries of battery EVs rose by a third from July to September.</p><p>It saw a big 213% jump in North America and a 60% rise in Europe of battery EVs.</p><p>But sales of battery EVs plunged by more than half in China.</p><p>One analyst said this was due to the varying market conditions in the three markets.</p><p>The results come a day after Volkswagen's Porsche unit said sales were down in China by more than a quarter in the first nine months of the year.</p><p>VW slashed its financial guidance for this year in September.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Volkswagen Group's release of new models paid off in the third quarter.</p><p>The German auto giant reported a 1% rise in deliveries during the period on Friday.</p><p>It said a boost from Europe and South America pushed back on pressure from China and the U.S..</p><p>Group deliveries to China fell 7%.</p><p>VW isn't&nbsp;the only German major to see a sales decline in the country recently.</p><p>Mercedes' was down by more than a quarter over the same period, while BMW also saw a slight drop.</p><p>Electric vehicles were a bright spot for VW in the third quarter.</p><p>Deliveries of battery EVs rose by a third from July to September.</p><p>It saw a big 213% jump in North America and a 60% rise in Europe of battery EVs.</p><p>But sales of battery EVs plunged by more than half in China.</p><p>One analyst said this was due to the varying market conditions in the three markets.</p><p>The results come a day after Volkswagen's Porsche unit said sales were down in China by more than a quarter in the first nine months of the year.</p><p>VW slashed its financial guidance for this year in September.</p></body>",
